  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In dehydrohalogenation reactions,&nbsp;the preferred product is that alkene which has the greater number of alkyl groups attached to the doubly bonded carbon atoms. Thus, 2-bromopentane gives pent-2-ene as the major product.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/83488d5f-42a2-4f47-9bed-c1a7ad154c16-7fc755fa-a43e-49f8-9496-f41827617b4f-a44d5f49-5106-4827-8a0f-ce21c19634a1-image.png\" style=\"width: 446px; height: 103px;\" />Rest all bromides are having only one type of beta hydrogen, hence, only one possible alkene is formed.</p>",
    "image": null
